I am now inside the spacious metro station.
There are many people here.
I go near the ticket counter.
There is a worker behind the counter.
I speak to him with respect.
"Hello, sir," I say.
"I need to get to a station near the sea by the metro train," I say.
"Is that station far?" I ask.
"No madam, that station is nearby," he says.
"Please give me a permanent metro card," I say.
"Okay madam," that worker says.
"Its price is one hundred rupees," he says.
I open my bag.
I give one hundred rupees to him.
He gives me a new permanent metro card.
I say thank you to him.
Now I have the metro card with me.
I happily go towards the entrance gate.
I board the metro train soon.
